from (values
('127.351.d.1.A',3,'A wind turbine, a power line, and a home thermostat are all parts of an:','["energy system", "grade book", "art gallery", "bus route"]'::jsonb,0,'Energy systems link production, delivery, and use.','original'),
('127.351.d.1.A',4,'Which job belongs to the electric power generation part of an energy system?','["Travel agent", "Power plant operator", "Pastry chef", "Court reporter"]'::jsonb,1,'Plant operators run generation equipment.','original'),
('127.351.d.1.B',3,'Looking at past employment trends helps a student:','["forget the past", "pick a lunch menu", "predict which energy jobs may be in demand", "choose a locker"]'::jsonb,2,'Trends guide career decisions.','original'),
('127.351.d.1.B',4,'When oil prices drop sharply, employment in drilling usually:','["stays exactly the same", "becomes illegal", "rises without limit", "falls as companies cut activity"]'::jsonb,3,'Low prices reduce drilling work.','original'),
('127.351.d.1.C',3,'Rising demand for electricity from data centers is a current issue because it:','["increases the need for new power supply", "ends energy use", "removes the grid", "lowers every bill"]'::jsonb,0,'More demand requires more supply.','original'),
('127.351.d.1.C',4,'Predicting future energy needs requires information about population growth, technology, and:','["movie releases", "economic activity", "school colors", "sports scores"]'::jsonb,1,'Economy drives energy demand.','original'),
('127.351.d.1.D',3,'A certification earned by passing an industry exam is called a:','["lunch ticket", "hall pass", "credential", "yearbook"]'::jsonb,2,'Credentials prove skills.','original'),
('127.351.d.1.D',4,'Starting your own solar installation company is an example of:','["retirement", "tenure", "unemployment", "entrepreneurship"]'::jsonb,3,'Entrepreneurs start businesses.','original'),
('127.351.d.1.E',3,'Using a spreadsheet to track a project''s materials and costs is applying skills with:','["resources and information", "yearbooks", "lunch menus", "bus maps"]'::jsonb,0,'Managing information and resources is a workplace competency.','original'),
('127.351.d.1.E',4,'A team leader divides a job into tasks and assigns them. This shows competency in organizing:','["recess games", "systems of operation", "school photos", "field day"]'::jsonb,1,'Organizing work is a systems skill.','original'),
('127.351.d.2.A',3,'Before a lab investigation with heating equipment, students should:','["skip the instructions", "eat in the lab", "review safety rules and wear protective gear", "remove all eye protection"]'::jsonb,2,'Safety comes first.','original'),
('127.351.d.2.A',4,'If a chemical spills in a lab, the correct first action is to:','["wipe it with bare hands", "leave quietly", "ignore it", "notify the teacher immediately"]'::jsonb,3,'Report spills right away.','original'),
('127.351.d.2.B',3,'A multimeter used in an energy lab measures:','["voltage, current, or resistance", "wind direction only", "height", "humidity only"]'::jsonb,0,'Multimeters measure electrical values.','original'),
('127.351.d.2.B',4,'A thermometer is the correct tool to find a liquid''s:','["voltage", "temperature", "pressure", "mass"]'::jsonb,1,'Thermometers measure temperature.','original'),
('127.351.d.2.C',3,'Building a small model generator and testing its output is a:','["guessing exercise", "memorization drill", "hands-on, minds-on activity", "lecture only"]'::jsonb,2,'Doing and thinking together builds understanding.','original'),
('127.351.d.2.C',4,'A group designs a test, records results, and explains why they happened. This mixes hands-on work with:','["copying", "avoidance", "random guessing", "conceptual reasoning"]'::jsonb,3,'Explaining results shows understanding.','original'),
('127.351.d.2.D',3,'Turning off lights in empty rooms is an example of:','["conserving resources", "drilling", "increasing demand", "wasting resources"]'::jsonb,0,'Conservation reduces use.','original'),
('127.351.d.2.D',4,'Reusing water at a plant for cooling more than once is an example of resource:','["speculation", "conservation", "contamination", "depletion"]'::jsonb,1,'Reuse reduces total use.','original'),
('127.351.d.3.A',3,'A student shares findings about solar output using a chart and a clear summary. This is:','["ignoring evidence", "hiding results", "communicating conclusions from data", "guessing"]'::jsonb,2,'Valid conclusions are supported by data.','original'),
('127.351.d.3.B',3,'The discovery of oil at Spindletop in 1901 had a large impact on:','["the building of canals", "the end of farming", "the invention of the telephone", "the growth of the Texas oil industry"]'::jsonb,3,'Spindletop launched the Texas oil boom.','original'),
('127.351.d.3.A',4,'A valid conclusion about an energy source must be based on:','["reliable evidence", "rumor", "advertising", "opinion alone"]'::jsonb,0,'Evidence supports valid conclusions.','original'),
('127.351.d.3.B',4,'The invention of the steam engine allowed factories to:','["stop using fuel", "use coal-powered machines instead of relying only on water or muscle", "avoid workers", "run without machines"]'::jsonb,1,'Steam power transformed industry.','original'),
('127.351.d.3.C',3,'A disadvantage of coal compared with natural gas is that coal generally:','["is a renewable resource", "needs no mining", "releases more carbon dioxide when burned", "burns without emissions"]'::jsonb,2,'Coal emits more CO2 per unit of energy.','original'),
('127.351.d.3.C',4,'An advantage of solar power is that it:','["uses uranium", "requires no equipment", "works only at night", "produces electricity without burning fuel"]'::jsonb,3,'Solar panels generate electricity from sunlight.','original'),
('127.351.d.3.D',3,'A decision that depends on testing hypotheses with evidence is a:','["scientific decision", "coin toss", "rumor", "hunch"]'::jsonb,0,'Science uses evidence and methods.','original'),
('127.351.d.3.D',4,'Deciding whether to build a power plant also involves public opinion, cost, and law, which are:','["only physical factors", "social and political factors", "only chemical factors", "irrelevant factors"]'::jsonb,1,'Not all decisions are purely scientific.','original'),
('127.351.d.4.A',3,'A good oral presentation about an energy issue should have:','["unrelated pictures", "only jokes", "a clear message supported by evidence", "no structure"]'::jsonb,2,'Clear structure and evidence persuade.','original'),
('127.351.d.4.A',4,'To communicate technical information to a general audience, a presenter should:','["use as much jargon as possible", "speak very quickly", "read silently", "use plain language and explain special terms"]'::jsonb,3,'Plain explanations help audiences.','original'),
('127.351.d.4.B',3,'A student downloads a table of annual oil production and makes a graph. This is:','["data retrieval and analysis", "data hiding", "data deletion", "data theft"]'::jsonb,0,'Retrieving and graphing data shows trends.','original'),
('127.351.d.4.B',4,'A data source about energy production is most reliable if it comes from:','["an anonymous post", "a government agency or well-known research organization", "an advertisement", "a rumor"]'::jsonb,1,'Reliable sources use documented methods.','original'),
('127.351.d.5.A',3,'Gasoline in a car mainly provides energy for:','["lighting", "cooling", "transportation", "cooking only"]'::jsonb,2,'Cars burn fuel to move.','original'),
('127.351.d.5.A',4,'Natural gas is used in homes mainly for:','["flying planes", "powering phones directly", "making glass only", "heating and cooking"]'::jsonb,3,'Homes use gas for heat and cooking.','original'),
('127.351.d.5.B',3,'In a flashlight, chemical energy in the battery is transformed into light and:','["thermal energy", "sound energy only", "nuclear energy", "gravitational energy only"]'::jsonb,0,'Bulbs also give off heat.','original'),
('127.351.d.5.B',4,'In a hydroelectric dam, the energy transformation is from the kinetic energy of falling water to:','["nuclear energy", "electrical energy", "chemical energy", "sound energy only"]'::jsonb,1,'Turbines turn motion into electricity.','original'),
('127.351.d.5.C',3,'Water stored behind a dam has potential energy because of:','["friction", "magnetism", "gravity", "sound"]'::jsonb,2,'Height in a gravitational field stores energy.','original'),
('127.351.d.5.C',4,'The potential energy of an object increases when it is:','["slowed", "cooled", "lowered", "lifted higher"]'::jsonb,3,'Height raises gravitational potential energy.','original'),
('127.351.d.5.D',3,'Work is calculated as force multiplied by:','["distance", "color", "time of day", "temperature"]'::jsonb,0,'W = F x d.','original'),
('127.351.d.5.D',4,'A 10 N force moves a box 3 meters. The work done is:','["3.3 J", "30 J", "7 J", "13 J"]'::jsonb,1,'10 x 3 = 30 joules.','original'),
('127.351.d.5.E',3,'Energy moving from a hot stove to a pan by direct contact is:','["radiation", "convection", "conduction", "reflection"]'::jsonb,2,'Conduction transfers heat by contact.','original'),
('127.351.d.5.E',4,'Heat from the sun reaches Earth across space by:','["friction", "conduction", "convection", "radiation"]'::jsonb,3,'Radiation needs no medium.','original'),
('127.351.d.5.F',3,'The law of conservation of energy says energy:','["cannot be created or destroyed, only transformed", "only exists in batteries", "is destroyed when used", "can be created from nothing"]'::jsonb,0,'Total energy is conserved.','original'),
('127.351.d.5.F',4,'A coal plant converts 35 percent of fuel energy to electricity. The remaining energy is mostly:','["lost from the universe", "released as waste heat", "created again", "destroyed"]'::jsonb,1,'Energy is conserved but spreads as heat.','original'),
('127.351.d.5.G',3,'A calorimeter is used to measure the:','["speed of wind", "mass of a planet", "energy released or absorbed in a reaction", "height of a building"]'::jsonb,2,'Calorimetry measures heat energy.','original'),
('127.351.d.5.G',4,'A food Calorie is a measure of:','["force", "distance", "voltage", "energy"]'::jsonb,3,'Calories measure energy content.','original'),
('127.351.d.6.A',3,'Which of these is a liquid fuel?','["Gasoline", "Uranium", "Coal", "Wood"]'::jsonb,0,'Gasoline is a liquid.','original'),
('127.351.d.6.A',4,'Propane and natural gas are examples of:','["nuclear fuels", "gaseous fuels", "solid fuels", "liquid metals"]'::jsonb,1,'They are stored and used as gases.','original'),
('127.351.d.6.B',3,'Drilling mud circulated in a well is used to:','["paint the rig", "cool the office", "carry cuttings to the surface and control pressure", "feed workers"]'::jsonb,2,'Mud removes cuttings and balances pressure.','original'),
('127.351.d.6.B',4,'Crude oil is moved over long distances most often by:','["bicycles", "balloons", "backpacks", "pipelines"]'::jsonb,3,'Pipelines move large volumes.','original'),
('127.351.d.6.C',3,'Capillary action allows a liquid to rise in a narrow space because of:','["adhesion and cohesion", "sound waves", "gravity alone", "magnetism"]'::jsonb,0,'Attraction to surfaces and between molecules pulls liquid up.','original'),
('127.351.d.6.C',4,'Capillary action helps oil move through the tiny pores of a rock, so it matters for:','["lighting a lamp only", "oil moving in a reservoir", "cooking food", "painting walls"]'::jsonb,1,'Pore spaces trap and move fluids.','original'),
('127.351.d.6.D',3,'If the temperature of a gas in a sealed rigid container rises, its pressure:','["stays zero", "disappears", "increases", "decreases"]'::jsonb,2,'Gay-Lussac: pressure rises with temperature.','original'),
('127.351.d.6.D',4,'According to Boyle''s law, squeezing a gas into a smaller volume at constant temperature makes the pressure:','["stay the same", "go down", "go to zero", "go up"]'::jsonb,3,'P and V are inversely related.','original'),
('127.351.d.7.A',3,'A map showing the sites of power plants in Texas helps a student see:','["where electricity is generated", "school bus stops", "ball fields", "grocery stores"]'::jsonb,0,'Maps show energy locations.','original'),
('127.351.d.7.A',4,'Texas has large wind farms mostly in:','["the Piney Woods only", "West Texas and the Panhandle", "downtown Austin only", "Houston harbor"]'::jsonb,1,'Strong, steady winds are in West Texas.','original'),
('127.351.d.7.B',3,'The East Texas oil field discovered in the 1930s led to:','["a drop in jobs", "a ban on drilling", "rapid growth in Texas oil production", "the end of oil"]'::jsonb,2,'It was one of the largest oil fields ever found.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
