('127.351.d.7.B',4,'Texas leads the nation in wind power and also in:','["banana production", "coffee production", "snow tourism", "crude oil production"]'::jsonb,3,'Texas is the top oil-producing state.','original'),
('127.351.d.7.C',3,'New drilling technology that lets operators reach oil across a wide area from one pad is:','["horizontal drilling", "tilling", "hand digging", "panning"]'::jsonb,0,'Horizontal wells reach more rock.','original'),
('127.351.d.7.C',4,'Battery storage helps wind and solar by:','["raising fuel costs", "saving power for when the sun and wind are not available", "stopping all generation", "replacing turbines"]'::jsonb,1,'Storage smooths supply.','original'),
('127.351.d.7.D',3,'One way a family can conserve energy is to:','["run empty appliances", "leave all lights on", "use LED bulbs", "open the fridge often"]'::jsonb,2,'LED bulbs use much less energy.','original'),
('127.351.d.7.D',4,'Sealing air leaks around windows helps a home save energy by reducing:','["sunlight", "gravity", "rainfall", "heat loss or gain"]'::jsonb,3,'Better insulation cuts heating and cooling use.','original'),
('127.351.d.7.E',3,'A map that shows major energy sources in Texas would include natural gas, wind, coal, and:','["nuclear power", "tidal power", "geysers", "volcanoes"]'::jsonb,0,'Texas has nuclear plants such as Comanche Peak.','original'),
('127.351.d.7.E',4,'Which Texas region has the largest oil production from the Permian Basin?','["East Texas coast", "West Texas", "South Padre Island", "Panhandle plains only"]'::jsonb,1,'The Permian Basin is in West Texas and eastern New Mexico.','original'),
('127.351.d.7.F',3,'The energy industry affects the Texas economy by providing:','["no taxes", "no jobs", "jobs and tax revenue", "only costs"]'::jsonb,2,'The industry supports many workers and public funds.','original'),
('127.351.d.7.F',4,'Oil and gas severance taxes in Texas help pay for:','["vacations", "private clubs", "sports teams", "public schools and highways"]'::jsonb,3,'Revenue is directed to state funds.','original'),
('127.351.d.7.G',3,'When demand for gasoline rises and supply stays the same, the price usually:','["goes up", "goes down", "freezes", "drops to zero"]'::jsonb,0,'More demand with limited supply raises prices.','original'),
('127.351.d.7.G',4,'A surplus of oil on the market with weak demand tends to:','["freeze the price", "push prices lower", "push prices higher", "end all drilling forever"]'::jsonb,1,'Oversupply lowers prices.','original'),
('127.351.d.7.H',3,'A rise in oil prices benefits oil-producing regions but can hurt:','["oil company profits", "drilling contractors", "consumers who pay more at the pump", "well owners"]'::jsonb,2,'Higher prices cost drivers more.','original'),
('127.351.d.7.H',4,'An economy that depends mostly on one energy source is most at risk when:','["it is sunny", "a holiday arrives", "school starts", "that source''s price falls sharply"]'::jsonb,3,'Dependence creates vulnerability.','original'),
('127.351.d.8.A',3,'Rock formed from cooled magma is called:','["igneous rock", "sedimentary rock", "metamorphic rock", "fossil"]'::jsonb,0,'Igneous rock forms from cooled magma or lava.','original'),
('127.351.d.8.A',4,'Oil and natural gas are most often found in:','["volcanic glass", "sedimentary rock", "granite", "igneous rock"]'::jsonb,1,'Sedimentary rocks have pore spaces.','original'),
('127.351.d.8.B',3,'Porosity describes the amount of:','["age of a rock", "color in a rock", "open space in a rock", "weight of a rock"]'::jsonb,2,'Porosity measures void space.','original'),
('127.351.d.8.B',4,'A rock that lets fluids flow easily through connected pores has high:','["hardness only", "density only", "opacity", "permeability"]'::jsonb,3,'Permeability measures flow ability.','original'),
('127.351.d.8.C',3,'An aquifer is an underground layer that:','["stores and transmits groundwater", "stores oil only", "contains only sand", "holds only air"]'::jsonb,0,'Aquifers hold usable groundwater.','original'),
('127.351.d.8.C',4,'The Ogallala is a major aquifer in the Texas:','["Gulf Coast beach", "Panhandle", "Big Bend desert", "Piney Woods"]'::jsonb,1,'The Ogallala lies beneath the High Plains.','original'),
('127.351.d.8.D',3,'Hydraulic fracturing uses high-pressure fluid to:','["cool a plant", "fill a pool", "crack rock and release trapped oil or gas", "paint a rig"]'::jsonb,2,'Fractures let hydrocarbons flow.','original'),
('127.351.d.8.D',4,'Proppant, such as sand, is pumped into fractures to:','["absorb oil permanently", "freeze the rock", "lower pressure", "keep the cracks open"]'::jsonb,3,'Proppant holds fractures open.','original'),
('127.351.d.9.A',3,'Which energy source is renewable?','["Wind", "Coal", "Petroleum", "Natural gas"]'::jsonb,0,'Wind replenishes naturally.','original'),
('127.351.d.9.A',4,'Non-renewable resources such as coal are called that because they:','["fall from the sky", "form over millions of years and are used faster than they form", "regrow each year", "are made in labs only"]'::jsonb,1,'They take geologic time to form.','original'),
('127.351.d.9.B',3,'Energy efficiency means getting:','["no work from energy", "energy from nothing", "more useful work from the same amount of energy", "less work from more energy"]'::jsonb,2,'Efficient systems waste less.','original'),
('127.351.d.9.B',4,'A typical natural gas combined-cycle plant is more efficient than an older coal plant because it:','["runs on batteries", "uses no turbine", "burns wood", "captures waste heat for extra power"]'::jsonb,3,'Combined cycle reuses exhaust heat.','original'),
('127.351.d.9.C',3,'A benefit of solar energy is that it produces:','["electricity with no direct emissions", "spilled oil", "nuclear waste", "smoke"]'::jsonb,0,'Solar panels emit nothing when operating.','original'),
('127.351.d.9.C',4,'A hazard associated with oil transport is the risk of:','["bird songs", "spills", "rainbows", "snow"]'::jsonb,1,'Spills can harm land and water.','original'),
('127.351.d.9.D',3,'Scrubbers installed on smokestacks reduce:','["fuel use only", "plant size", "harmful air emissions", "noise only"]'::jsonb,2,'Scrubbers remove pollutants.','original'),
('127.351.d.9.D',4,'Planting native vegetation on a restored mine site helps reduce:','["fuel prices", "wind speed", "solar output", "erosion and habitat loss"]'::jsonb,3,'Reclamation protects soil and wildlife.','original'),
('127.351.d.9.E',3,'A landowner, an energy company, and a conservation group may disagree about a project because they have different:','["viewpoints and priorities", "favorite colors", "birthdays", "phone numbers"]'::jsonb,0,'Stakeholders weigh costs and benefits differently.','original'),
('127.351.d.9.E',4,'A fair discussion of an energy source considers cost, availability, and:','["only slogans", "environmental effects", "only rumors", "only advertising"]'::jsonb,1,'A balanced view looks at tradeoffs.','original'),
('127.351.d.9.F',3,'Sunlight is considered a renewable source because it:','["is stored in oil fields", "runs out quickly", "is replenished continuously", "is mined"]'::jsonb,2,'The sun supplies energy daily.','original'),
('127.351.d.9.F',4,'Uranium is considered non-renewable because its supply on Earth is:','["made of wind", "created daily", "unlimited", "finite"]'::jsonb,3,'Ore deposits are limited.','original'),
('127.351.d.9.G',3,'Public concern about climate change has increased demand for:','["low-carbon energy options", "more coal exclusively", "slower technology", "fewer jobs"]'::jsonb,0,'Social views influence energy choices.','original'),
('127.351.d.9.G',4,'When a new scientific finding changes public attitudes about an energy source, policy makers may:','["ban science", "change regulations or incentives", "ignore all data", "stop voting"]'::jsonb,1,'Public views affect policy.','original'),
('127.351.d.10.A',3,'Burning fossil fuels adds which gas to the atmosphere?','["Argon", "Helium", "Carbon dioxide", "Neon"]'::jsonb,2,'Combustion releases CO2.','original'),
('127.351.d.10.A',4,'Surface coal mining can disturb land by removing:','["gravity", "moonlight", "sound waves", "soil and vegetation"]'::jsonb,3,'Mining changes the landscape.','original'),
('127.351.d.10.B',3,'Deciding whether to drill in a protected wildlife area raises an:','["ethical issue", "spelling issue", "lunch issue", "arithmetic issue"]'::jsonb,0,'It involves values and trade-offs.','original'),
('127.351.d.10.B',4,'An argument for responsible resource use says that current generations should leave resources and a healthy environment for:','["no one", "future generations", "only today''s owners", "only businesses"]'::jsonb,1,'Stewardship considers the future.','original'),
('127.351.d.10.C',3,'A long-term disadvantage of a fossil fuel is that its supply is:','["silent", "free", "limited", "unlimited"]'::jsonb,2,'Fossil fuels are finite.','original'),
('127.351.d.10.C',4,'A long-term advantage of wind power is that its fuel supply is:','["radioactive", "expensive", "rare", "free and does not run out"]'::jsonb,3,'Wind is renewable.','original'),
('127.351.d.10.D',3,'Access to reliable electricity improves quality of life by supporting:','["lighting, refrigeration, and health care", "only distance", "only taxes", "only noise"]'::jsonb,0,'Energy powers basic services.','original'),
('127.351.d.10.D',4,'In communities without electricity, children often have difficulty:','["finding sunlight", "studying after dark", "growing taller", "hearing sounds"]'::jsonb,1,'Lighting extends study time.','original'),
('127.351.d.10.E',3,'Moving electricity from power plants to homes over long distances uses:','["coal cars only", "water slides", "transmission lines", "school buses"]'::jsonb,2,'High-voltage lines carry power.','original'),
('127.351.d.10.E',4,'Transformers are used in the power grid to:','["cool the sun", "grow crops", "store oil", "raise or lower voltage"]'::jsonb,3,'Transformers step voltage up or down.','original'),
('127.351.d.10.F',3,'The Clean Air Act is a law passed by the United States to limit:','["air pollution", "school start times", "road signs", "tax rates"]'::jsonb,0,'The act regulates air pollutants.','original'),
('127.351.d.10.F',4,'The Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) is responsible for:','["running schools", "enforcing federal environmental regulations", "setting gas prices", "building homes"]'::jsonb,1,'The EPA writes and enforces environmental rules.','original'),
('127.351.d.11.A',3,'Before inviting a guest speaker from the energy industry, students should:','["ignore the topic", "ask about the speaker''s home address", "prepare questions about the speaker''s career", "skip the visit"]'::jsonb,2,'Preparation makes the visit useful.','original'),
('127.351.d.11.A',4,'A good source for finding energy professionals for a classroom visit is:','["a stranger online", "an unrelated store", "a random stranger", "a local industry association or utility"]'::jsonb,3,'Associations connect schools with professionals.','original'),
('127.351.d.11.B',3,'A museum about oil history, such as the Texas Energy Museum, helps students learn about:','["how energy was found, produced, and used", "fashion trends", "movie plots", "sports records"]'::jsonb,0,'Museums preserve energy history.','original'),
