('127.352.d.1.B',3,'An offshore drilling platform is used to:','["grow crops", "load trains", "drill wells in the ocean", "build roads"]'::jsonb,2,'Offshore rigs reach sea-floor reservoirs.','original'),
('127.352.d.1.B',4,'The part of a rig that rotates the drill string is called the:','["windsock", "cafeteria", "bunkhouse", "rotary table or top drive"]'::jsonb,3,'The rotary system turns the pipe.','original'),
('127.352.d.1.C',3,'Directional drilling allows operators to:','["steer a well toward a target that is not directly below the rig", "avoid drilling", "paint the well", "only drill straight down"]'::jsonb,0,'Wells can be steered.','original'),
('127.352.d.1.C',4,'A mud motor in directional drilling helps by:','["measuring prices", "turning the bit without rotating the whole drill string", "cooling the crew", "lighting the rig"]'::jsonb,1,'Mud motors rotate the bit downhole.','original'),
('127.352.d.1.D',3,'Fishing in a well means:','["repairing boats", "selling fish", "retrieving lost tools or pipe from the borehole", "catching trout"]'::jsonb,2,'Fishing recovers stuck equipment.','original'),
('127.352.d.1.D',4,'A tool used to catch the top of a lost pipe in a well is called an:','["anchor", "umbrella", "bottle", "overshot"]'::jsonb,3,'Overshots grip the outside of the fish.','original'),
('127.352.d.1.E',3,'Casing is run in a well to:','["protect the hole and isolate formations", "feed the crew", "hold tools", "cool the rig"]'::jsonb,0,'Casing lines the well.','original'),
('127.352.d.1.E',4,'Cement is pumped around the casing to:','["warm the rock", "seal it and prevent fluid from moving between zones", "lower pressure only", "color the pipe"]'::jsonb,1,'Cement isolates zones.','original'),
('127.352.d.1.F',3,'Fluid pressure in a well is commonly measured in:','["degrees only", "feet", "pounds per square inch (psi)", "gallons"]'::jsonb,2,'psi is the common unit.','original'),
('127.352.d.1.F',4,'If the pressure of drilling mud is too low compared with formation pressure, the well could experience a:','["holiday", "picnic", "nap", "kick"]'::jsonb,3,'Underbalance can let formation fluids enter.','original'),
('127.352.d.1.G',3,'Flow in a new well may be started by:','["perforating the casing and, if needed, reducing pressure in the well", "painting the wellhead", "shutting everything", "adding sand to the sea"]'::jsonb,0,'Perforations open the pay zone.','original'),
('127.352.d.1.G',4,'When a reservoir has too little pressure to flow naturally, operators may use:','["a fan", "artificial lift such as a pump", "a blanket", "a bucket"]'::jsonb,1,'Pumps lift fluid to the surface.','original'),
('127.352.d.1.H',3,'The Christmas tree on a producing well controls:','["crew meals", "lighting of the rig", "the flow of fluids at the surface", "office air"]'::jsonb,2,'The tree has valves that control flow.','original'),
('127.352.d.1.H',4,'Tubing is the pipe inside the casing that:','["stores water", "lights the rig", "holds crew", "carries oil and gas to the surface"]'::jsonb,3,'Production tubing carries fluid.','original'),
('127.352.d.1.I',3,'Perforating a casing means:','["making holes so oil or gas can enter the well", "bending it", "painting it", "burying it"]'::jsonb,0,'Perforations connect well to formation.','original'),
('127.352.d.1.I',4,'After perforating, a well may be stimulated with acid or fracturing to:','["decrease production", "improve flow from the formation", "fill it with water", "close the well"]'::jsonb,1,'Stimulation increases productivity.','original'),
('127.352.d.1.J',3,'A packer is placed in a well completion to:','["store cash", "measure wind", "seal the space between tubing and casing", "feed the crew"]'::jsonb,2,'Packers isolate zones.','original'),
('127.352.d.1.J',4,'The plan that lists the equipment to be installed in a finished well is the:','["yearbook", "bus map", "lunch plan", "completion design"]'::jsonb,3,'Completion designs list tubing, packers, and tools.','original'),
('127.352.d.1.K',3,'A well log is a record of:','["measurements taken in the wellbore", "office rent", "fuel prices", "crew birthdays"]'::jsonb,0,'Logs record rock and fluid properties.','original'),
('127.352.d.1.K',4,'A gamma ray log helps identify:','["oil price", "rock types such as shale", "crew size", "wind speed"]'::jsonb,1,'Shale gives higher gamma readings.','original'),
('127.352.d.1.L',3,'A well that produces less than expected may be checked for problems such as:','["a bus delay", "a school holiday", "damage near the wellbore or low reservoir pressure", "bad weather in another state"]'::jsonb,2,'Analysts examine skin, pressure, and equipment.','original'),
('127.352.d.1.L',4,'Scale or paraffin buildup in tubing can cause a well to:','["produce more", "turn to water", "stop needing pressure", "produce less"]'::jsonb,3,'Deposits restrict flow.','original'),
('127.352.d.1.M',3,'A roughneck on a drilling rig works mainly on the:','["rig floor handling pipe and equipment", "sales floor", "bank counter", "office desk"]'::jsonb,0,'Roughnecks handle the pipe.','original'),
('127.352.d.1.M',4,'A good worker on a drilling crew must be able to:','["work alone only", "follow safety rules and work as a team", "avoid training", "ignore directions"]'::jsonb,1,'Safety and teamwork are essential.','original'),
('127.352.d.2.A',3,'Major equipment at a production site includes separators, tanks, and:','["sports gear", "cafeteria trays", "wellhead and pumps", "swing sets"]'::jsonb,2,'These are standard production items.','original'),
('127.352.d.2.A',4,'A separator at a production facility divides well fluid into oil, gas, and:','["smoke", "salt only", "sand only", "water"]'::jsonb,3,'Separators split the three phases.','original'),
('127.352.d.2.B',3,'Valves on the wellhead are used to:','["control the flow of fluids", "warm the crew", "paint the pipe", "count visitors"]'::jsonb,0,'Valves open and close flow.','original'),
('127.352.d.2.B',4,'The valve on a wellhead used to shut off flow in an emergency is the:','["kitchen valve", "master valve", "garden valve", "party valve"]'::jsonb,1,'The master valve is the main shutoff.','original'),
('127.352.d.2.C',3,'Following the process flow means tracing fluid from the wellhead through:','["a bakery", "a school", "separators, treaters, and storage", "a classroom"]'::jsonb,2,'The flow runs through processing equipment.','original'),
('127.352.d.2.C',4,'After separation, the gas is usually sent to a:','["pool", "school", "garden", "pipeline or processing plant"]'::jsonb,3,'Gas is sold through pipelines.','original'),
('127.352.d.2.D',3,'The wellhead is the equipment at the top of a well that:','["supports the casing and tubing and controls flow", "paints the rig", "holds the office", "stores crew meals"]'::jsonb,0,'It anchors and controls the well.','original'),
('127.352.d.2.D',4,'The casing head and tubing head are parts of the:','["flare", "wellhead", "mud pit", "rig floor"]'::jsonb,1,'These form the wellhead assembly.','original'),
('127.352.d.2.E',3,'A choke on a wellhead is used to:','["measure time", "increase noise", "regulate the rate of flow", "cool the crew"]'::jsonb,2,'Chokes restrict flow to control rate and pressure.','original'),
('127.352.d.2.E',4,'A pressure gauge on the wellhead lets operators:','["watch TV", "listen to music", "count trucks", "monitor well pressure"]'::jsonb,3,'Gauges show pressure.','original'),
('127.352.d.2.F',3,'Compared with a land wellhead, a subsea wellhead must be:','["designed for high pressure and underwater use", "left unprotected", "smaller than a pencil", "made of paper"]'::jsonb,0,'Subsea equipment faces deep-water conditions.','original'),
('127.352.d.2.F',4,'A high-pressure wellhead is built stronger than a low-pressure one because it must:','["hold less", "withstand higher internal pressures", "weigh less", "cost less"]'::jsonb,1,'Rating matches expected pressure.','original'),
('127.352.d.2.G',3,'A key difference between onshore and offshore facilities is that offshore sites:','["have no weather", "need no safety", "are located at sea and have limited space", "have unlimited space"]'::jsonb,2,'Platforms are compact and remote.','original'),
('127.352.d.2.G',4,'Supplies to an offshore platform are often delivered by:','["train", "bicycle", "school bus", "boat or helicopter"]'::jsonb,3,'Boats and helicopters serve platforms.','original'),
('127.352.d.2.H',3,'The Gulf of Mexico is known as a major region for:','["offshore oil and gas production", "wheat farming", "diamond mining", "skiing"]'::jsonb,0,'The Gulf is a leading offshore area.','original'),
('127.352.d.2.H',4,'The Marcellus Shale is a major natural gas region located in the:','["Southwest desert", "northeastern United States", "Pacific Northwest", "Hawaii"]'::jsonb,1,'It lies under Pennsylvania and nearby states.','original'),
('127.352.d.2.I',3,'Hydrogen sulfide (H2S) is dangerous because it is:','["a food additive", "a harmless vapor", "a toxic gas that can be deadly", "a bottled drink"]'::jsonb,2,'H2S is highly toxic.','original'),
('127.352.d.2.I',4,'Workers in areas where H2S may be present should carry:','["a radio only", "a lunch box only", "a camera", "a personal gas monitor"]'::jsonb,3,'Monitors alert workers to gas.','original'),
('127.352.d.2.J',3,'If a wellhead leaks, the problem can affect:','["the flowlines and facilities connected to it", "only the weather", "only another planet", "only the moon"]'::jsonb,0,'Production systems are linked.','original'),
('127.352.d.2.J',4,'A pressure drop at the wellhead can signal a problem in the:','["sports team", "connected pipeline or equipment", "grocery store", "school bell"]'::jsonb,1,'Connected systems reveal issues.','original'),
('127.352.d.2.K',3,'Monitoring a well includes regularly checking:','["sports scores", "school grades", "pressure, temperature, and flow rate", "lunch menus"]'::jsonb,2,'Production data are tracked.','original'),
('127.352.d.2.K',4,'Automated sensors that send well data to a control room are part of:','["a classroom game", "a bus line", "a mail route", "SCADA monitoring"]'::jsonb,3,'SCADA collects and sends data remotely.','original'),
('127.352.d.2.L',3,'A pumper is a worker who:','["visits wells to check equipment and record data", "teaches school", "bakes bread", "drives a taxi"]'::jsonb,0,'Pumpers inspect and maintain well sites.','original'),
('127.352.d.2.L',4,'Routine wellhead maintenance includes greasing valves and:','["painting murals", "checking for leaks", "repainting the sun", "moving mountains"]'::jsonb,1,'Preventive maintenance finds problems early.','original'),
('127.352.d.2.M',3,'Using a computer simulator to practice operating a wellhead is useful because it:','["removes the need for training", "pays the trainee", "lets trainees learn without real-world risk", "replaces all safety rules"]'::jsonb,2,'Simulators make training safer.','original'),
('127.352.d.2.M',4,'When troubleshooting, the first step is usually to:','["guess", "shut down everything immediately", "ignore alarms", "gather data and identify symptoms"]'::jsonb,3,'Good troubleshooting starts with data.','original'),
('127.352.d.2.N',3,'A manual shutdown is usually required when:','["an unsafe condition such as a leak is detected", "it is lunch time", "the weather is nice", "a visitor arrives"]'::jsonb,0,'Unsafe conditions warrant shutdown.','original'),
('127.352.d.2.N',4,'An automatic safety valve closes when:','["the sun rises", "pressure goes outside safe limits", "a bird passes", "the radio plays"]'::jsonb,1,'Safety devices respond to abnormal pressure.','original'),
('127.352.d.3.A',3,'Personal protective equipment on a well site includes a hard hat, safety glasses, and:','["sandals", "flip-flops", "steel-toed boots", "bare feet"]'::jsonb,2,'Boots protect feet.','original'),
('127.352.d.3.A',4,'Flame-resistant clothing is worn to protect workers from:','["rain only", "cold only", "noise only", "fire and flash hazards"]'::jsonb,3,'FR clothing resists burning.','original'),
('127.352.d.3.B',3,'OSHA is the federal agency that sets and enforces:','["workplace safety standards", "tax rates", "road names", "school schedules"]'::jsonb,0,'OSHA protects workers.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
