from (values
('127.352.d.3.B',4,'The Bureau of Safety and Environmental Enforcement (BSEE) regulates safety for:','["school buses", "offshore oil and gas operations", "airports", "food trucks"]'::jsonb,1,'BSEE oversees offshore operations.','original'),
('127.353.d.1.A',3,'Before pipelines, crude oil was moved in:','["satellites", "jet planes", "wooden barrels by wagon", "electric cars"]'::jsonb,2,'Early oil moved in barrels.','original'),
('127.353.d.1.A',4,'Pipelines became popular because they:','["cost more than wagons", "need no maintenance", "are the slowest method", "move large volumes of oil cheaply and safely"]'::jsonb,3,'Pipelines are efficient.','original'),
('127.353.d.1.B',3,'Oil is transported over land by pipeline, rail, and:','["tanker truck", "hot air balloon", "bicycle", "horse"]'::jsonb,0,'Trucks move oil short distances.','original'),
('127.353.d.1.B',4,'A benefit of moving crude oil by rail is that it:','["uses no fuel", "can reach places that have no pipeline", "needs no tracks", "is silent"]'::jsonb,1,'Rail adds flexibility.','original'),
('127.353.d.1.C',3,'A hazard communication program tells workers about:','["school grades", "sports teams", "dangers of chemicals they handle", "lunch menus"]'::jsonb,2,'HazCom informs workers.','original'),
('127.353.d.1.C',4,'Drivers of crude oil tank trucks must follow rules from the:','["School Board", "Department of Music", "Department of Art", "Department of Transportation"]'::jsonb,3,'DOT regulates hauling.','original'),
('127.353.d.1.D',3,'Crude oil prices are affected by supply, demand, and:','["global events", "lunch choices", "hair styles", "school colors"]'::jsonb,0,'World events move prices.','original'),
('127.353.d.1.D',4,'When OPEC members agree to cut production, oil prices tend to:','["freeze", "rise", "fall", "vanish"]'::jsonb,1,'Lower supply raises prices.','original'),
('127.353.d.1.E',3,'Refined products such as gasoline reach consumers through:','["school hallways", "museums", "distribution terminals and service stations", "libraries"]'::jsonb,2,'Terminals supply stations.','original'),
('127.353.d.1.E',4,'Wholesale sales of fuel are made to businesses, while retail sales are made to:','["no one", "planets", "governments only", "individual consumers"]'::jsonb,3,'Retail serves the public.','original'),
('127.353.d.1.F',3,'Exploration companies create new oil and gas supplies by:','["finding and drilling new reserves", "selling gas", "refining gas", "buying gas"]'::jsonb,0,'They add supply.','original'),
('127.353.d.1.F',4,'Service companies support drilling by providing:','["groceries", "equipment, crews, and technical services", "clothing", "school books"]'::jsonb,1,'Service firms support operators.','original'),
('127.353.d.1.G',3,'An independent oil company usually focuses on:','["teaching", "refining, shipping, and retail", "exploration and production only", "manufacturing toys"]'::jsonb,2,'Independents specialize in upstream work.','original'),
('127.353.d.1.G',4,'A company that explores, produces, refines, and sells products is called:','["isolated", "inactive", "independent", "integrated"]'::jsonb,3,'Integrated firms span the chain.','original'),
('127.353.d.1.H',3,'Before investing in a drilling prospect, investors consider risk, cost, and:','["expected return", "school colors", "bus route", "lunch menu"]'::jsonb,0,'They weigh return against risk.','original'),
('127.353.d.1.H',4,'A dry hole is a well that:','["never gets drilled", "finds no commercial oil or gas", "produces too much", "is on land"]'::jsonb,1,'Dry holes are financial losses.','original'),
('127.353.d.1.I',3,'An investment of $1,000,000 that returns $1,200,000 earned what percent gain?','["120 percent", "12 percent", "20 percent", "2 percent"]'::jsonb,2,'Gain of 200,000 divided by 1,000,000 is 20 percent.','original'),
('127.353.d.1.I',4,'A project costs $500,000 and yields $50,000 profit in a year. The rate of return is:','["50 percent", "5 percent", "1 percent", "10 percent"]'::jsonb,3,'50,000 / 500,000 = 10 percent.','original'),
('127.353.d.2.A',3,'Drilling cuttings and waste fluids are managed by:','["hauling to approved disposal sites or recycling", "burning in schoolyards", "burying near homes", "pouring in creeks"]'::jsonb,0,'Wastes follow disposal rules.','original'),
('127.353.d.2.A',4,'A lined pit is used to:','["hold crew", "contain waste fluids and prevent seepage into soil", "store money", "grow plants"]'::jsonb,1,'Liners protect soil and groundwater.','original'),
('127.353.d.2.B',3,'Booms are placed on water after an oil spill to:','["raise prices", "start fires", "contain and limit the spread of oil", "feed fish"]'::jsonb,2,'Booms corral oil.','original'),
('127.353.d.2.B',4,'Skimmers are used in spill response to:','["cool the sea", "warm the sea", "add oil", "remove oil from the water surface"]'::jsonb,3,'Skimmers recover oil.','original'),
('127.353.d.2.C',3,'Refineries reduce environmental impact by capturing:','["vapors and emissions with control equipment", "wastewater", "more smoke", "fuel"]'::jsonb,0,'Control devices limit releases.','original'),
('127.353.d.2.C',4,'Recycling water within a refinery reduces:','["safety", "freshwater withdrawal", "production", "oil quality"]'::jsonb,1,'Reuse conserves water.','original'),
('127.353.d.3.A',3,'A petroleum company that invests in solar and wind projects is exploring:','["less power", "only oil", "renewable energy sources", "more coal only"]'::jsonb,2,'Many firms diversify.','original'),
('127.353.d.3.A',4,'Biofuels such as ethanol are made from:','["uranium", "crude oil only", "coal only", "plant materials"]'::jsonb,3,'Ethanol comes from crops like corn.','original'),
('127.353.d.3.B',3,'A major challenge for the petroleum industry is meeting demand while:','["reducing emissions", "raising emissions", "ignoring rules", "ending jobs"]'::jsonb,0,'Balance demand and environment.','original'),
('127.353.d.3.B',4,'Price swings are a challenge because they make it hard to:','["tell time", "plan investments", "see colors", "build roads"]'::jsonb,1,'Volatility affects planning.','original'),
('127.353.d.3.C',3,'Carbon capture and storage is a technology that:','["burns more coal", "makes more CO2", "traps carbon dioxide before it enters the atmosphere", "drains lakes"]'::jsonb,2,'CCS reduces emissions.','original'),
('127.353.d.3.C',4,'Advanced batteries could help the energy system by:','["wasting electricity", "ending the grid", "removing power lines", "storing electricity for later use"]'::jsonb,3,'Storage balances supply and demand.','original'),
('127.353.d.3.D',3,'A nontechnical way to reduce energy demand is to:','["change habits, such as carpooling", "leave lights on", "idle cars", "build bigger engines"]'::jsonb,0,'Behavior changes cut use.','original'),
('127.353.d.3.D',4,'Building codes that require better insulation are an example of:','["a weather event", "a policy solution to reduce energy use", "a toy", "a new planet"]'::jsonb,1,'Policies can lower demand.','original'),
('127.354.d.1.A',3,'Hydraulic fracturing has been used by service companies such as Halliburton since the:','["1700s", "2020s", "late 1940s", "1800s"]'::jsonb,2,'Commercial fracturing began in 1949.','original'),
('127.354.d.1.A',4,'Pioneers of modern horizontal shale development include Mitchell Energy in the:','["Hawaii coast", "Alaska ice", "Sahara Desert", "Barnett Shale of Texas"]'::jsonb,3,'Mitchell Energy developed Barnett Shale fracturing.','original'),
('127.354.d.1.B',3,'Hydraulic fracturing became important to US energy because it made it possible to produce oil and gas from:','["tight shale formations", "open lakes", "deserts", "oceans"]'::jsonb,0,'Fracturing unlocked shale.','original'),
('127.354.d.1.B',4,'Combining hydraulic fracturing with horizontal drilling led to a rapid increase in:','["wind power only", "US oil and gas production", "coal mining only", "solar power only"]'::jsonb,1,'The combination drove the shale boom.','original'),
('127.354.d.1.C',3,'Hydraulic technology in oil fields helped North America become:','["an importer of all fuel", "a nuclear-only country", "one of the world''s largest oil and gas producers", "a coal-free nation"]'::jsonb,2,'The US became a leading producer.','original'),
('127.354.d.1.C',4,'An impact of shale development on energy prices has been:','["no change", "ending of gas use", "higher gas prices only", "lower natural gas prices for consumers"]'::jsonb,3,'More supply lowered prices.','original'),
('127.354.d.1.D',3,'New oil and natural gas production from shale supports North American:','["energy independence and jobs", "unemployment", "school closures", "fuel shortages only"]'::jsonb,0,'It increased domestic supply.','original'),
('127.354.d.1.D',4,'Increased natural gas production has led many power plants to switch from:','["hydro to oil", "coal to natural gas", "wind to coal", "gas to coal"]'::jsonb,1,'Cheap gas replaced coal in many plants.','original'),
('127.354.d.2.A',3,'A pneumatic system uses:','["magnets", "flowing oil", "compressed air to do work", "sunlight"]'::jsonb,2,'Pneumatics use compressed gas.','original'),
('127.354.d.2.A',4,'A pneumatic system needs an air compressor, a receiver tank, and:','["a diary", "a paintbrush", "a lunchbox", "valves and actuators"]'::jsonb,3,'These are functional components.','original'),
('127.354.d.2.B',3,'Pneumatic pressure is most commonly measured in:','["psi", "feet", "seconds", "pounds"]'::jsonb,0,'psi is pounds per square inch.','original'),
('127.354.d.2.B',4,'Atmospheric pressure at sea level is about:','["0 psi", "14.7 psi", "147 psi", "1.47 psi"]'::jsonb,1,'Standard atmosphere is 14.7 psi.','original'),
('127.354.d.2.C',3,'A hydraulic system uses:','["magnets", "air only", "a liquid under pressure to transmit force", "sunlight"]'::jsonb,2,'Hydraulics use incompressible fluid.','original'),
('127.354.d.2.C',4,'A hydraulic system typically has a reservoir, a pump, valves, and:','["a lamp", "a pencil", "a clock", "an actuator such as a cylinder"]'::jsonb,3,'Actuators do the work.','original'),
('127.354.d.2.D',3,'Hydraulic pressure is measured in:','["psi", "meters per second", "ohms", "volts"]'::jsonb,0,'psi is a pressure unit.','original'),
('127.354.d.2.D',4,'Hydraulics is the study of how liquids:','["make sound", "transmit force and motion", "grow plants", "change color"]'::jsonb,1,'Fluids transmit force.','original'),
('127.354.d.3.A',3,'A basic safety rule in pneumatics is to always wear:','["sandals", "headphones only", "safety glasses", "sunglasses"]'::jsonb,2,'Eye protection is required.','original'),
('127.354.d.3.A',4,'Before disconnecting pneumatic components, you should first:','["ignore the gauge", "tighten fittings", "raise the pressure", "release the pressure from the system"]'::jsonb,3,'Depressurize before service.','original'),
