('127.354.d.4.A',3,'A double-acting pneumatic cylinder uses air pressure to move the piston in:','["both directions", "a circle only", "no direction", "one direction only"]'::jsonb,0,'Air extends and retracts the rod.','original'),
('127.354.d.4.A',4,'Compared with a single-acting cylinder, a double-acting cylinder does not rely on a:','["valve", "return spring", "compressor", "hose"]'::jsonb,1,'Air does the return stroke.','original'),
('127.354.d.4.B',3,'A five-way three-position valve can route air to extend, retract, or:','["melt the cylinder", "paint the cylinder", "hold or stop the cylinder", "blow the whistle"]'::jsonb,2,'The center position stops or holds.','original'),
('127.354.d.4.B',4,'A directional control valve is used to:','["measure time", "warm the room", "hold paper", "change the path of air flow"]'::jsonb,3,'Valves direct flow.','original'),
('127.354.d.4.C',3,'A quick-connect fitting allows hoses to be:','["connected and disconnected without tools", "painted", "permanently glued", "welded together"]'::jsonb,0,'Quick-connects speed assembly.','original'),
('127.354.d.4.C',4,'A quick-connect fitting usually has a:','["lock of hair", "sleeve that locks the plug in place", "bell", "candle"]'::jsonb,1,'The sleeve holds the connection.','original'),
('127.354.d.4.D',3,'Before connecting a quick-connect to a pressurized supply, you should:','["cut the hose", "do nothing", "make sure the circuit is set up and the supply is off or low", "stand on the hose"]'::jsonb,2,'Safe connection starts with controlled pressure.','original'),
('127.354.d.4.D',4,'After connecting a pneumatic circuit, you should check for:','["noise from the sky", "paint", "gloves", "air leaks"]'::jsonb,3,'Leaks waste air and cause hazards.','original'),
('127.354.d.5.A',3,'ISO symbols on a hydraulic schematic represent:','["components such as pumps and cylinders", "paintings", "stars", "words in a poem"]'::jsonb,0,'Symbols show standard parts.','original'),
('127.354.d.5.A',4,'Lines on a hydraulic schematic show:','["cloud shapes", "the paths fluid takes", "sports scores", "the weather"]'::jsonb,1,'Lines represent fluid conductors.','original'),
('127.354.d.5.B',3,'A hydraulic schematic should show the pump, valve, cylinder, and:','["television", "bicycle", "reservoir", "swimming pool"]'::jsonb,2,'The reservoir is part of the circuit.','original'),
('127.354.d.5.B',4,'When drawing a schematic, you should label:','["only the colors", "only the date", "only the page", "each component and the flow direction"]'::jsonb,3,'Labels improve clarity.','original'),
('127.354.d.6.A',3,'Force equals pressure multiplied by:','["area", "time", "height", "speed"]'::jsonb,0,'F = P x A.','original'),
('127.354.d.6.A',4,'A cylinder with a piston area of 4 square inches and 1,000 psi produces a force of:','["250 pounds", "4,000 pounds", "996 pounds", "1,004 pounds"]'::jsonb,1,'4 x 1,000 = 4,000.','original'),
('127.354.d.6.B',3,'Pascal''s Law says pressure applied to a confined fluid is transmitted:','["not at all", "only downward", "equally throughout the fluid", "only upward"]'::jsonb,2,'Pressure is transmitted equally.','original'),
('127.354.d.6.B',4,'A hydraulic jack lifts a heavy car by using Pascal''s Law to:','["hide force", "delete force", "destroy force", "multiply force"]'::jsonb,3,'A small piston force produces a larger output.','original'),
('127.354.d.6.C',3,'A hydraulic pump converts mechanical energy into:','["fluid flow and pressure", "sound", "light", "heat only"]'::jsonb,0,'Pumps move fluid.','original'),
('127.354.d.6.C',4,'A hydraulic motor converts fluid power into:','["sound", "rotating mechanical motion", "food", "light"]'::jsonb,1,'Motors produce rotation.','original'),
('127.354.d.6.D',3,'A single-acting hydraulic cylinder uses fluid to move in:','["a circle", "both directions with fluid", "one direction, returning by spring or load", "no direction"]'::jsonb,2,'The return is not powered by fluid.','original'),
('127.354.d.6.D',4,'A double-acting hydraulic cylinder can push and:','["only rest", "only float", "only spin", "pull with fluid power"]'::jsonb,3,'Fluid powers both strokes.','original'),
('127.355.d.1.A',3,'The well completion phase prepares a drilled well to:','["produce oil or gas", "be abandoned", "sell lunch", "grow crops"]'::jsonb,0,'Completion makes the well productive.','original'),
('127.355.d.1.A',4,'Hydrocarbons are made accessible by connecting the wellbore to the pay zone through:','["umbrellas", "perforations", "insulation", "painting"]'::jsonb,1,'Perforations connect formation and well.','original'),
('127.355.d.1.B',3,'Computer modeling is used in completion design to:','["replace all equipment", "guess randomly", "predict well performance and test options", "ignore data"]'::jsonb,2,'Models help compare designs.','original'),
('127.355.d.1.B',4,'A completion engineer uses reservoir data to decide on:','["fashion", "lunch menus", "bus times", "the best way to produce the well"]'::jsonb,3,'Design is data driven.','original'),
('127.355.d.1.C',3,'An open hole completion leaves the producing section:','["uncased", "buried", "fully cased", "flooded with cement"]'::jsonb,0,'Open hole has no casing across the pay zone.','original'),
('127.355.d.1.C',4,'Sand control completions keep formation sand from:','["improving oil", "entering the well and damaging equipment", "lighting the rig", "adding oil"]'::jsonb,1,'Screens and gravel packs block sand.','original'),
('127.355.d.1.D',3,'A conventional completion typically includes casing, tubing, and:','["a sign", "a tire", "a packer", "a tent"]'::jsonb,2,'A packer seals the annulus.','original'),
('127.355.d.1.D',4,'Tubing is run inside casing so that fluids:','["leave the well", "burn", "freeze", "flow through a smaller, controlled path"]'::jsonb,3,'Tubing carries produced fluids.','original'),
('127.355.d.2.A',3,'Health and safety standards for well sites are designed to:','["protect workers and the environment", "slow work for no reason", "increase accidents", "reduce wages"]'::jsonb,0,'Standards prevent harm.','original'),
('127.355.d.2.A',4,'A job safety analysis (JSA) is done before a task to:','["set prices", "identify hazards and plan controls", "pick teams", "order food"]'::jsonb,1,'JSAs reduce risk.','original'),
('127.355.d.2.B',3,'A tool used to measure depth of the well in completions is a:','["mixer", "paintbrush", "wireline tool", "bicycle pump"]'::jsonb,2,'Wireline tools run in the well.','original'),
('127.355.d.2.B',4,'Blowout preventers (BOPs) are used to:','["start the engine", "cool the crew", "lower the flag", "control well pressure and prevent uncontrolled flow"]'::jsonb,3,'BOPs seal the well.','original'),
('127.355.d.2.C',3,'Spending more on safety training usually helps a company avoid:','["costly accidents and downtime", "profit", "growth", "income"]'::jsonb,0,'Safety saves money.','original'),
('127.355.d.2.C',4,'A serious well-site accident can cost a company in injuries, fines, and:','["free fuel", "lost production and reputation", "new friends", "extra holidays"]'::jsonb,1,'Accidents have large costs.','original'),
('127.355.d.3.A',3,'Drilling mud helps the drilling process by:','["shortening the well", "painting the rig", "cooling the bit and carrying cuttings to the surface", "feeding the crew"]'::jsonb,2,'Mud has several functions.','original'),
('127.355.d.3.A',4,'A generic well design includes surface casing, intermediate casing, and:','["roof shingles", "sails", "paint", "production casing"]'::jsonb,3,'These are typical casing strings.','original'),
('127.355.d.3.B',3,'Cuttings produced during drilling are usually moved to a disposal area by:','["trucks or pipelines to an approved site", "boats to schools", "bicycles", "balloons"]'::jsonb,0,'Cuttings require proper disposal.','original'),
('127.355.d.3.B',4,'A platform well is drilled from a:','["classroom", "fixed or floating structure at sea", "barn", "stadium"]'::jsonb,1,'Platforms support offshore wells.','original'),
('127.355.d.3.C',3,'A reservoir formation is important because it:','["grows crops", "makes the weather", "holds the oil or gas", "keeps time"]'::jsonb,2,'The reservoir stores hydrocarbons.','original'),
('127.355.d.3.C',4,'Evaluating a formation helps decide whether a well is:','["loud", "old", "pretty", "commercially worth completing"]'::jsonb,3,'Economics depend on the formation.','original'),
('127.355.d.4.A',3,'A safety plan for a well site should include emergency procedures and:','["protective equipment requirements", "bus routes", "lunch menus", "art projects"]'::jsonb,0,'Plans cover people and procedures.','original'),
('127.355.d.4.A',4,'Before starting high-pressure work, the crew holds a meeting to review:','["fashion", "hazards and responsibilities", "movies", "sports"]'::jsonb,1,'Pre-job meetings improve safety.','original'),
('127.355.d.4.B',3,'A flow meter measures:','["wind color", "temperature of the sun", "how much fluid moves through a line", "noise level"]'::jsonb,2,'Meters quantify flow.','original'),
('127.355.d.4.B',4,'Oil, gas, and water flows from a well are typically separated and measured at the:','["parking lot", "classroom", "gift shop", "separator"]'::jsonb,3,'Separators measure phases.','original'),
('127.355.d.4.C',3,'Surface well testing must include steps to prevent:','["uncontrolled releases and fires", "sunlight", "good weather", "wind"]'::jsonb,0,'Precautions protect crews.','original'),
('127.355.d.4.C',4,'During flowback, workers should keep ignition sources away because gas can be:','["cold", "flammable", "blue", "sweet"]'::jsonb,1,'Natural gas can ignite.','original'),
('127.355.d.4.D',3,'Knowing the surroundings before well work helps workers avoid:','["lunch", "weekends", "hazards such as power lines and neighbors", "rain"]'::jsonb,2,'Site awareness prevents accidents.','original'),
('127.355.d.4.D',4,'Wells near homes or streams require extra care to protect:','["only fuel", "only the crew", "only equipment", "people and water resources"]'::jsonb,3,'Environmental sensitivity matters.','original'),
('127.355.d.5.A',3,'Core analysis is performed on rock samples to learn about:','["porosity and permeability", "weather", "sound", "popularity"]'::jsonb,0,'Cores reveal reservoir properties.','original'),
('127.355.d.5.A',4,'A core is a cylinder of rock that is:','["buried", "cut and brought to the surface for study", "painted", "melted"]'::jsonb,1,'Cores are physical samples.','original'),
('127.355.d.5.B',3,'Core analysis data are combined with well logs to:','["slow drilling", "raise prices", "better understand the reservoir", "remove casing"]'::jsonb,2,'Combining data improves interpretation.','original'),
('127.355.d.5.B',4,'High porosity and permeability in a core suggest the rock can:','["be useless", "not store fluids", "only hold air", "store and produce fluids well"]'::jsonb,3,'Both properties support production.','original'),
('127.355.d.5.C',3,'Well logging uses instruments lowered into the well to measure:','["rock and fluid properties", "student grades", "lunch cost", "bus routes"]'::jsonb,0,'Logging tools record data.','original'),
('127.355.d.5.C',4,'Resistivity logs help identify zones containing:','["clouds", "hydrocarbons rather than salt water", "students", "books"]'::jsonb,1,'Hydrocarbons resist electric current.','original'),
('127.355.d.5.D',3,'Formation testing can include collecting:','["maps of the moon", "food orders", "fluid and pressure samples from the formation", "school pictures"]'::jsonb,2,'Testers sample fluids and measure pressure.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
insert into public.question_bank (teks_code, teks_item_id, subject, grade_num, course, difficulty, qtype, prompt, choices, answer_idx, explanation, source, status, gen_batch)
select distinct on (v.prompt) v.code, i.id, d.subject,
       case when i.grade_level = 'K' then 0 when i.grade_level ~ '^[0-9]+' then substring(i.grade_level from '^[0-9]+')::smallint end,
       case when i.grade_level is null then i.grade_course_title end,
       v.diff, 'mc', v.prompt, v.choices, v.ans, v.expl, v.src, 'checked', 'cte_56_v1'
from (values
('127.355.d.5.D',4,'A formation tester is run in a well to measure:','["the weather", "surface traffic", "cell service", "pressure and fluid samples at selected depths"]'::jsonb,3,'Testers confirm productivity.','original'),
('127.355.d.5.E',3,'A drill stem test (DST) is run to:','["test the flow potential of a formation", "train students", "cool the crew", "paint the rig"]'::jsonb,0,'DSTs flow the formation briefly.','original'),
('127.355.d.5.E',4,'A drill stem test uses a tool string run on:','["a garden hose", "the drill pipe", "a kite string", "a rope ladder"]'::jsonb,1,'The test tools are on drill pipe.','original'),
('127.355.d.5.F',3,'DST results help engineers determine how much fluid will flow and at what:','["size of the crew", "taste", "pressure", "color"]'::jsonb,2,'They measure flow and pressure.','original'),
('127.355.d.5.F',4,'A DST that shows strong flow rates would suggest the formation is:','["useless", "dry for sure", "made of glass", "likely productive"]'::jsonb,3,'Flow indicates productivity.','original'),
('127.355.d.5.G',3,'The cost of a completion includes equipment, labor, and:','["services such as logging and perforating", "parties", "prizes", "tickets"]'::jsonb,0,'Completion costs add up.','original'),
('127.355.d.5.G',4,'A company compares completion costs with expected production to decide if the well is:','["pretty", "economically viable", "fun", "famous"]'::jsonb,1,'Economics drive decisions.','original'),
('127.356.d.1.A',3,'Industries that use process technology include chemical plants, refineries, and:','["movie theaters", "bakeries only", "power plants", "toy stores"]'::jsonb,2,'Process operators work in these plants.','original'),
('127.356.d.1.A',4,'A process technician in a refinery works to monitor:','["retail sales", "grocery shelves", "school buses", "units that turn crude oil into products"]'::jsonb,3,'Technicians monitor refining units.','original'),
('127.356.d.1.B',3,'A process operator monitors equipment, records data, and:','["responds to alarms", "drives a bus", "paints houses", "teaches art"]'::jsonb,0,'Operators watch and control the process.','original'),
('127.356.d.1.B',4,'An entry-level process technology job typically requires:','["a PhD", "a high school diploma and often an associate degree", "no education", "a law degree"]'::jsonb,1,'Many programs offer two-year degrees.','original'),
('127.356.d.1.C',3,'Technical vocabulary such as valve, flow, and temperature should be:','["ignored", "misspelled", "used correctly when communicating on the job", "avoided"]'::jsonb,2,'Clear terms prevent mistakes.','original'),
('127.356.d.1.C',4,'Accurate shift logs are important because they:','["add noise", "waste time", "entertain readers", "pass information to the next shift"]'::jsonb,3,'Logs communicate status.','original'),
('127.356.d.1.D',3,'Automation and artificial intelligence are emerging issues because they change:','["how plants are controlled and staffed", "the calendar", "the moon", "the weather"]'::jsonb,0,'Technology changes plant work.','original'),
('127.356.d.1.D',4,'Cybersecurity is an emerging issue for process plants because control systems can be:','["lost", "targeted by hackers", "painted", "muted"]'::jsonb,1,'Connected systems face threats.','original'),
('127.356.d.1.E',3,'An instrument that measures temperature in a pipe is a:','["stopwatch", "telescope", "thermocouple", "compass"]'::jsonb,2,'Thermocouples sense temperature.','original'),
('127.356.d.1.E',4,'A transmitter sends a signal from a sensor to a:','["mailbox", "playground", "bakery", "control room"]'::jsonb,3,'Signals travel to controllers.','original'),
('127.356.d.2.A',3,'A valve that allows flow in only one direction is a:','["check valve", "bicycle valve", "garden valve", "party valve"]'::jsonb,0,'Check valves prevent backflow.','original'),
('127.356.d.2.A',4,'A centrifugal pump moves fluid by:','["magnet only", "spinning an impeller", "rubbing sticks", "freezing it"]'::jsonb,1,'Impellers add energy to fluid.','original'),
('127.356.d.2.B',3,'A piping and instrumentation diagram (P&ID) shows:','["a school map", "a family tree", "pipes, equipment, and instruments in a process", "a menu"]'::jsonb,2,'P&IDs are process maps.','original'),
('127.356.d.2.B',4,'On a P&ID, a circle with letters such as TI usually represents:','["a clock", "a ball game", "a lunch tray", "an instrument such as a temperature indicator"]'::jsonb,3,'Circles show instruments.','original'),
('127.356.d.3.A',3,'A block flow diagram gives a:','["simple overview of a process", "detailed wiring plan", "floor plan of a house", "recipe for cookies"]'::jsonb,0,'It shows major steps.','original'),
('127.356.d.3.A',4,'A process flow diagram (PFD) is more detailed than a block diagram and shows major:','["clothing", "equipment and flow streams", "music", "hair styles"]'::jsonb,1,'PFDs list equipment and flows.','original'),
('127.356.d.3.B',3,'A circuit schematic uses standard symbols to show:','["clouds", "plants", "electrical components and connections", "recipes"]'::jsonb,2,'Schematics show circuits.','original'),
('127.356.d.3.C',3,'Building quality, reliability, and safety into a process begins with:','["skipping checks", "random changes", "ignoring alarms", "good design and preventive maintenance"]'::jsonb,3,'Design and maintenance prevent failures.','original'),
('127.356.d.3.C',4,'Statistical process control is used to:','["detect when a process drifts from its target", "find friends", "decorate", "raise prices"]'::jsonb,0,'SPC monitors variation.','original'),
('127.356.d.3.D',3,'Voltage, current, and resistance are related by:','["Murphy''s law", "Ohm''s law", "Newton''s law", "Boyle''s law"]'::jsonb,1,'V = I x R.','original'),
('127.356.d.3.D',4,'A circuit with 12 volts and 4 ohms of resistance has a current of:','["16 amps", "48 amps", "3 amps", "8 amps"]'::jsonb,2,'I = V / R = 12 / 4 = 3.','original'),
('127.356.d.4.A',3,'Lockout/tagout is a safety procedure that prevents:','["lunch breaks", "phone calls", "weather", "equipment from starting during maintenance"]'::jsonb,3,'It isolates energy sources.','original'),
('127.356.d.4.A',4,'Confined space entry requires a permit, gas testing, and:','["an attendant outside", "a party", "music", "a nap"]'::jsonb,0,'Confined spaces are hazardous.','original'),
('127.356.d.4.B',3,'A safety data sheet (SDS) lists information about a chemical''s:','["price only", "hazards and safe handling", "color only", "movie rating"]'::jsonb,1,'SDSs communicate hazards.','original'),
('127.356.d.4.B',4,'Standard operating procedures should be followed:','["whenever convenient", "only on Mondays", "exactly as written unless changed through proper approval", "never"]'::jsonb,2,'Procedures protect people.','original'),
('127.356.d.4.C',3,'Improper maintenance can lead to equipment failure, injuries, and:','["clean air", "extra holidays", "good luck", "environmental releases"]'::jsonb,3,'Failures can harm people and environment.','original'),
('127.356.d.4.C',4,'Skipping a required inspection is an example of:','["negligence", "precision", "innovation", "teamwork"]'::jsonb,0,'Negligence is failing to do required work.','original'),
('127.356.d.4.D',3,'A micrometer or caliper is used to:','["weigh ships", "measure small dimensions precisely", "carry water", "play music"]'::jsonb,1,'Precision tools measure size.','original'),
('127.356.d.4.D',4,'Calibrating an instrument ensures it:','["looks new", "costs less", "gives accurate readings", "makes noise"]'::jsonb,2,'Calibration checks accuracy.','original'),
('127.356.d.4.E',3,'The agency that sets workplace safety rules in the United States is:','["NASA", "NBA", "FIFA", "OSHA"]'::jsonb,3,'OSHA regulates worker safety.','original'),
('127.356.d.4.E',4,'The EPA is most concerned with protecting:','["the environment", "sports leagues", "stock prices", "television ratings"]'::jsonb,0,'EPA enforces environmental rules.','original'),
('127.356.d.5.A',3,'A technician computes the volume of a rectangular tank by multiplying length by width by:','["name", "height", "age", "color"]'::jsonb,1,'V = l x w x h.','original'),
('127.356.d.5.A',4,'A tank is 4 ft long, 3 ft wide, and 2 ft deep. Its volume is:','["12 cubic feet", "9 cubic feet", "24 cubic feet", "14 cubic feet"]'::jsonb,2,'4 x 3 x 2 = 24.','original'),
('127.356.d.5.B',3,'A reading of 0.25 gallons expressed as a fraction is:','["1/2", "2/5", "1/8", "1/4"]'::jsonb,3,'0.25 = 1/4.','original'),
('127.356.d.5.B',4,'To add 1/2 and 0.25, a technician may convert both to:','["decimals or fractions with a common form", "times", "colors", "names"]'::jsonb,0,'Use consistent forms.','original'),
('127.356.d.5.C',3,'Measurement uncertainty is caused by factors such as:','["music", "instrument limits and reading errors", "luck", "moonlight"]'::jsonb,1,'Every measurement has uncertainty.','original'),
('127.356.d.5.C',4,'Using a more precise instrument usually makes uncertainty:','["larger", "negative", "smaller", "random"]'::jsonb,2,'Better instruments reduce uncertainty.','original'),
('127.356.d.5.D',3,'In the order of operations, calculations in parentheses are done:','["never", "last", "only once", "first"]'::jsonb,3,'Parentheses come first.','original'),
('127.356.d.5.D',4,'What is 2 + 3 x 4?','["14", "9", "20", "24"]'::jsonb,0,'Multiply first: 3x4 = 12, plus 2 = 14.','original'),
('127.356.d.5.E',3,'The cross-sectional area of a round pipe is found with the formula for the area of a:','["triangle", "circle", "square", "line"]'::jsonb,1,'A = pi r squared.','original'),
