('127.356.d.6.B',3,'When evaluating information for a problem, a technician should check whether it is:','["colorful", "old", "long", "accurate and relevant"]'::jsonb,3,'Quality information supports decisions.','original'),
('127.356.d.6.B',4,'Data from an instrument that has not been calibrated should be:','["treated with caution", "used for all decisions", "trusted blindly", "hidden"]'::jsonb,0,'Uncalibrated data may be wrong.','original'),
('127.356.d.6.C',3,'Fishbone diagrams and the 5 Whys are tools for finding:','["dates", "root causes", "lunch spots", "friends"]'::jsonb,1,'They help trace causes.','original'),
('127.356.d.6.C',4,'Comparing several possible solutions before choosing is part of:','["fear", "delay", "critical thinking", "guessing"]'::jsonb,2,'Critical thinkers weigh options.','original'),
('127.356.d.6.D',3,'Technical research for a decision may use manuals, standards, and:','["rumors", "gossip", "jokes", "manufacturer data"]'::jsonb,3,'Authoritative sources are best.','original'),
('127.356.d.6.D',4,'Before changing a process, a technician should research whether the change is:','["safe and approved", "quick", "cheap only", "fun"]'::jsonb,0,'Management of change requires approval.','original'),
('127.356.d.7.A',3,'A simple model of a process system, such as a tank and pump setup, can be built to:','["replace the plant", "test ideas safely", "skip training", "save no time"]'::jsonb,1,'Models allow safe testing.','original'),
('127.356.d.7.A',4,'A computer simulation of a distillation column allows trainees to:','["shut down actual plants", "avoid learning", "practice operations without real risk", "remove all rules"]'::jsonb,2,'Simulations are safe practice.','original'),
('127.356.d.7.B',3,'A student adjusts the valve in a mockup to raise the tank level to a goal. This shows how to:','["ignore the goal", "avoid the task", "destroy the model", "achieve a goal using a simple model"]'::jsonb,3,'Mockups teach control.','original'),
('127.356.d.7.B',4,'In a level control loop, the controller opens or closes a valve to keep the level:','["at a set point", "at maximum always", "at zero", "random"]'::jsonb,0,'Controllers hold set points.','original'),
('127.356.d.7.C',3,'Executing a mockup includes starting equipment in the correct:','["time zone", "sequence", "language", "color"]'::jsonb,1,'Sequence matters.','original'),
('127.356.d.7.C',4,'After executing a mockup, the team should compare results to:','["the bus schedule", "the lunch menu", "the goal", "the weather"]'::jsonb,2,'Results are compared to the goal.','original'),
('127.356.d.7.D',3,'Choosing the right safety equipment for a task depends on:','["the color of the helmet", "the time", "the weather forecast", "the hazards present"]'::jsonb,3,'Hazards drive PPE selection.','original'),
('127.356.d.7.D',4,'Chemical splash goggles are chosen over regular safety glasses when:','["liquids may splash into the eyes", "it is sunny", "it is dark", "the work is quiet"]'::jsonb,0,'Goggles seal against splashes.','original'),
('127.356.d.7.E',3,'Calculations in process work often involve flow, temperature, and:','["fashion", "pressure", "fame", "flavor"]'::jsonb,1,'These are core variables.','original'),
('127.356.d.7.E',4,'To convert 5,280 feet to miles, you should divide by:','["52.8", "1,000", "5,280", "12"]'::jsonb,2,'There are 5,280 feet in a mile.','original'),
('127.356.d.7.F',3,'Trends on a control room display help operators see:','["the weather", "the news", "the clock only", "how a variable changes over time"]'::jsonb,3,'Trends show history.','original'),
('127.356.d.7.F',4,'An alarm on a control screen means that a measurement has crossed:','["a limit", "a street", "a line in a book", "a border"]'::jsonb,0,'Alarms signal limit violations.','original'),
('127.356.d.7.G',3,'Simulations help build critical thinking by letting trainees:','["avoid decisions", "troubleshoot problems and see the results", "guess only", "watch movies"]'::jsonb,1,'Practice builds judgment.','original'),
('127.356.d.7.G',4,'During a simulated upset, the best response is to:','["shut everything randomly", "ignore the alarm", "follow procedures and diagnose systematically", "panic"]'::jsonb,2,'Systematic response works best.','original'),
('127.356.d.8.A',3,'A conclusion is valid when it is:','["popular", "loud", "based on opinion only", "supported by the data"]'::jsonb,3,'Valid conclusions follow from data.','original'),
('127.356.d.8.A',4,'A small sample size can weaken a conclusion because it may:','["not represent the whole", "be too exact", "be too colorful", "be too large"]'::jsonb,0,'Small samples are less reliable.','original'),
('127.356.d.8.B',4,'A table is useful for recording data because it:','["removes data", "organizes values for comparison", "adds noise", "hides values"]'::jsonb,1,'Tables organize data.','original'),
('127.357.d.1.A',3,'The agency that regulates workplace safety in the United States is:','["NBA", "NASA", "OSHA", "FIFA"]'::jsonb,2,'OSHA regulates worker safety.','original'),
('127.357.d.1.A',4,'The Texas Railroad Commission regulates the Texas:','["school buses", "banks", "airlines", "oil and gas industry"]'::jsonb,3,'The RRC oversees oil and gas.','original'),
('127.357.d.1.B',3,'OSHA''s Process Safety Management standard applies to facilities that handle:','["highly hazardous chemicals", "only food", "only paper", "only toys"]'::jsonb,0,'PSM covers hazardous chemicals.','original'),
('127.357.d.1.B',4,'A worker who sees a violation of a safety standard should:','["hide it", "report it through the proper channel", "ignore it", "post it online only"]'::jsonb,1,'Reporting protects workers.','original'),
('127.357.d.1.C',3,'Safety programs used along the Gulf Coast often include training such as:','["art class", "dance class", "H2S awareness and first aid", "cooking class"]'::jsonb,2,'Industry sites require this training.','original'),
('127.357.d.1.C',4,'A site safety orientation is given to:','["only students", "no one", "only managers", "all new workers and visitors"]'::jsonb,3,'Everyone must know site rules.','original'),
('127.357.d.1.D',3,'A hot work permit is required before:','["welding or cutting near flammable materials", "reading", "walking", "eating"]'::jsonb,0,'Permits control ignition sources.','original'),
('127.357.d.1.D',4,'A permit-to-work system is an administrative control that:','["pays workers", "authorizes and documents hazardous work", "orders lunch", "schedules breaks"]'::jsonb,1,'Permits manage risk.','original'),
('127.357.d.1.E',3,'Eyewash stations must be:','["locked", "removed", "tested regularly and kept clear", "hidden"]'::jsonb,2,'They must work in emergencies.','original'),
('127.357.d.1.E',4,'A gas detector alarm means workers should:','["silence it", "go closer", "ignore it", "follow emergency procedures and move to a safe area"]'::jsonb,3,'Alarms require action.','original'),
('127.357.d.1.F',3,'An engineering control such as a ventilation system:','["removes hazards at the source", "stops work", "replaces PPE completely", "causes hazards"]'::jsonb,0,'Engineering controls reduce exposure.','original'),
('127.357.d.1.F',4,'Guards on rotating machinery are an example of:','["a schedule", "an engineering control", "a lunch break", "a company party"]'::jsonb,1,'Guards physically separate people.','original'),
('127.357.d.1.G',3,'Personal protective equipment that protects hearing is:','["gloves", "a hat", "earplugs or earmuffs", "sunglasses"]'::jsonb,2,'Hearing protection reduces noise.','original'),
('127.357.d.1.G',4,'PPE is considered the last line of defense because it:','["replaces training", "is always perfect", "is optional", "does not remove the hazard"]'::jsonb,3,'Controls at the source are preferred.','original'),
('127.357.d.1.H',3,'A noise dosimeter measures a worker''s:','["noise exposure", "weight", "height", "speed"]'::jsonb,0,'Dosimeters track noise levels.','original'),
('127.357.d.1.H',4,'Hearing protection is generally required when noise exposure averages above:','["60 decibels", "85 decibels", "20 decibels", "40 decibels"]'::jsonb,1,'The action level is 85 dBA for 8 hours.','original'),
('127.357.d.1.I',4,'A supplied-air respirator is used when the atmosphere is:','["cool", "pleasant", "immediately dangerous to life or health", "bright"]'::jsonb,2,'IDLH atmospheres require supplied air.','original'),
('127.357.d.1.J',3,'Process operators use portable gas monitors to detect:','["weather", "traffic", "music", "hazardous gases"]'::jsonb,3,'Monitors detect toxic and flammable gases.','original'),
('127.357.d.1.J',4,'Four-gas monitors commonly detect oxygen, combustible gas, H2S, and:','["carbon monoxide", "helium", "radon", "neon"]'::jsonb,0,'CO is a common fourth sensor.','original'),
('127.357.d.2.A',3,'A spill is when a liquid is accidentally released, while a release can also include:','["water vapor only", "gases or vapors", "music", "light"]'::jsonb,1,'Releases include gases.','original'),
('127.357.d.2.A',4,'Wind direction matters during a release because it:','["changes the price", "moves the moon", "carries vapors toward or away from people", "delays lunch"]'::jsonb,2,'Evacuate crosswind or upwind.','original'),
('127.357.d.2.B',3,'Secondary containment, such as a dike around a tank, helps:','["start a spill", "feed workers", "warm tanks", "contain a spill"]'::jsonb,3,'Dikes hold leaked fluid.','original'),
('127.357.d.2.B',4,'An emergency shutdown system (ESD) is designed to:','["stop a process quickly during an emergency", "increase pressure", "start a spill", "begin production"]'::jsonb,0,'ESDs bring plants to safe condition.','original'),
('127.357.d.2.C',3,'The Occupational Safety and Health Administration is part of the:','["Department of Music", "Department of Labor", "Department of Sports", "Department of Art"]'::jsonb,1,'OSHA is under the Department of Labor.','original'),
('127.357.d.2.C',4,'The EPA, OSHA, and the Coast Guard are examples of:','["school clubs", "sports leagues", "government regulatory agencies", "music groups"]'::jsonb,2,'They enforce rules.','original'),
('127.357.d.2.D',3,'HAZCOM requires employers to label hazardous chemicals, provide safety data sheets, and:','["raise pay", "close sites", "stop work", "train workers"]'::jsonb,3,'Labels, SDSs, and training are the core.','original'),
('127.357.d.2.D',4,'A container label under HazCom includes a signal word such as:','["Danger or Warning", "Maybe", "Goodbye", "Hello"]'::jsonb,0,'Signal words show severity.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
insert into public.question_bank (teks_code, teks_item_id, subject, grade_num, course, difficulty, qtype, prompt, choices, answer_idx, explanation, source, status, gen_batch)
select distinct on (v.prompt) v.code, i.id, d.subject,
       case when i.grade_level = 'K' then 0 when i.grade_level ~ '^[0-9]+' then substring(i.grade_level from '^[0-9]+')::smallint end,
       case when i.grade_level is null then i.grade_course_title end,
       v.diff, 'mc', v.prompt, v.choices, v.ans, v.expl, v.src, 'checked', 'cte_56_v1'
from (values
('127.357.d.2.E',3,'The three elements needed for a fire are fuel, oxygen, and:','["wind", "heat", "sound", "water"]'::jsonb,1,'The fire triangle has three elements.','original'),
('127.357.d.2.E',4,'A vapor cloud explosion can occur when flammable vapors mix with air and find:','["a cool breeze", "dry soil", "an ignition source", "water"]'::jsonb,2,'Ignition causes explosion.','original'),
('127.357.d.2.F',3,'The Maritime Transportation Security Act (MARSEC) is designed to protect ports and vessels from:','["low pay", "bad weather", "lunch", "terrorism and security threats"]'::jsonb,3,'MARSEC addresses security threats.','original'),
('127.357.d.2.F',4,'Access control at a port facility often includes credentials such as the:','["TWIC card", "gift card", "membership card", "library card"]'::jsonb,0,'TWIC is required for secure areas.','original'),
('127.357.d.3.A',3,'Lockout/tagout protects workers from hazardous:','["gossip", "stored energy", "sunshine", "lunch"]'::jsonb,1,'Stored energy can injure.','original'),
('127.357.d.3.A',4,'A slip, trip, and fall hazard on a work surface can be reduced by:','["removing lights", "using oil", "keeping walkways clean and dry", "adding clutter"]'::jsonb,2,'Housekeeping prevents falls.','original'),
('127.357.d.3.B',3,'Before working at height, a worker should wear:','["headphones", "sandals", "a necktie", "a fall protection harness"]'::jsonb,3,'Fall protection is required above six feet in construction.','original'),
('127.357.d.3.B',4,'A hazard when operating vehicles on a well site is:','["limited visibility and heavy equipment traffic", "no equipment", "no traffic", "perfect visibility"]'::jsonb,0,'Sites are busy.','original'),
('127.357.d.3.C',3,'Lightning storms at a petroleum site require workers to:','["hold metal", "stop outdoor work and seek shelter", "climb towers", "work faster"]'::jsonb,1,'Lightning is deadly.','original'),
('127.357.d.3.C',4,'High winds can adversely affect safety by making crane lifts:','["easier", "quieter", "unsafe", "faster"]'::jsonb,2,'Wind limits lifting.','original'),
('127.357.d.4.A',3,'Toxic chemicals released into air or water are examples of:','["school supplies", "food", "toys", "environmental pollutants"]'::jsonb,3,'Pollutants harm ecosystems.','original'),
('127.357.d.4.A',4,'Benzene is a toxic chemical found in petroleum that is also a:','["known carcinogen", "flavor", "vitamin", "nutrient"]'::jsonb,0,'Benzene causes cancer.','original'),
('127.357.d.4.B',3,'A Material Safety Data Sheet (MSDS), now called an SDS, lists a product''s:','["country of origin only", "hazards and first aid measures", "color of the label", "price"]'::jsonb,1,'SDSs describe safe handling.','original'),
('127.357.d.4.B',4,'Section 4 of an SDS describes:','["employee names", "company history", "first-aid measures", "storage prices"]'::jsonb,2,'First aid is Section 4.','original'),
('127.357.d.4.C',3,'Under the Toxic Substances Control Act, a new chemical must be reviewed by the EPA before:','["it is bought", "it is named", "it is tested only", "it is manufactured or sold"]'::jsonb,3,'EPA reviews new chemicals.','original'),
('127.357.d.4.C',4,'A company that wants to manufacture a new chemical submits to the EPA a:','["premanufacture notice", "lunch menu", "school form", "postcard"]'::jsonb,0,'A PMN begins the review.','original'),
('127.357.d.4.D',3,'Before production begins at a new site, an operator must obtain:','["a pet", "required permits from regulators", "a trophy", "a picture"]'::jsonb,1,'Permits are required.','original'),
('127.357.d.4.D',4,'An air quality permit is required to control:','["traffic lights", "student behavior", "emissions from the site", "school grades"]'::jsonb,2,'Air permits limit emissions.','original'),
('127.357.d.4.E',3,'A spill prevention plan reduces the chance of:','["boredom", "hunger", "rain", "oil reaching soil or water"]'::jsonb,3,'Plans prevent releases.','original'),
('127.357.d.4.E',4,'Storm water controls such as berms help keep pollutants from reaching:','["streams and rivers", "gas stations", "stores", "classrooms"]'::jsonb,0,'Controls protect water.','original'),
('127.356.d.3.B',4,'On an industry circuit schematic, two parallel lines of unequal length usually mark a:','["resistor", "battery or cell", "ground wire", "switch"]'::jsonb,1,'The long and short plates are the battery symbol.','original'),
('127.356.d.8.B',4,'A bar graph is the best way to compare the monthly output of four different pumps because it:','["only lists names", "hides the differences", "shows separate categories side by side", "shows change over many years"]'::jsonb,2,'Bar graphs compare categories.','original'),
('127.357.d.1.I',4,'A filtering air-purifying respirator is NOT suitable when the air has too little:','["odor", "dust", "moisture", "oxygen"]'::jsonb,3,'Filters do not supply oxygen; supplied air is needed.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
